# tcpdrill, the receiver's silly window avoidance floor.
#
# RFC 1122 4.2.3.3: the receiver must not advertise a window increment smaller
# than min(MSS, RCV.BUFF/2).  Only the RCV.BUFF/2 term was implemented, so on
# this stack's window, 8 KB to 33 KB, w01 in tcp.drill bounds it, the
# smallest window update that could ever leave was between 4 KB and 16 KB.  A
# sender whose window had run down to a few hundred bytes had to wait for the
# application to read half the buffer before it heard otherwise, when one
# segment's worth of room is all it needs to carry on.
#
# WHAT THESE TWO CASES SEPARATE.  s01 reads exactly one segment and asserts the
# window update; before the MSS floor it did not come out.  s02 reads a hundred
# bytes and asserts that nothing does, which is the half of the rule that has to
# survive, an update per byte read is the silly window itself.
#
# THE ACKNOWLEDGEMENT NUMBER DOES NOT MOVE across the read, because a read
# changes the window and nothing else.  That is what makes the frame a window
# update rather than a data acknowledgment, and it is why these cases assert an
# ACK carrying an acknowledgement number that has already been sent once.
#
# NEITHER CASE HAS EVER BEEN RUN.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

# Two full segments in, one read out.  The receive queue still holds the second,
# so the window is credited by what was read rather than reset to the default,
# and the credit is exactly one MSS, the floor, and nothing above it.
case s01_reading_one_segment_updates_the_window
socket
connect
tx S seq=0
rx SA seq=0 ack=1 win=8192 mss=1460
tx A seq=1 ack=1
rx PA seq=1 ack=1 len=1460
tx A seq=1 ack=1461 within=400
rx PA seq=1461 ack=1 len=1460
tx A seq=1 ack=2921 within=400
recv 1460 = 1460
tx A seq=1 ack=2921 within=400

# A hundred bytes read is not an update.  Both segments are small so that the
# read cannot reach the floor from below.
case s02_reading_less_than_a_segment_is_not_an_update
socket
connect
tx S seq=0
rx SA seq=0 ack=1 win=8192 mss=1460
tx A seq=1 ack=1
rx PA seq=1 ack=1 len=100
tx A seq=1 ack=101 within=400
rx PA seq=101 ack=1 len=100
tx A seq=1 ack=201 within=400
recv 100 = 100
notx 500
